---
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Claim from '../components/Claim.astro';
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
import MccChart from '../components/MccChart.astro';
import ConfusionGrid from '../components/ConfusionGrid.astro';
import photo from '../assets/avnish.jpg';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { papers, posts } from '../data/content';

const origin = Astro.site ?? new URL('http://localhost:4321');
const avatar = await getImage({ src: photo, width: 480, format: 'jpg' });

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: site.name,
  url: origin.href,
  image: new URL(avatar.src, origin).href,
  email: `mailto:${site.email}`,
  description: site.description,
  affiliation: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: site.school },
  address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Lucknow', addressCountry: 'IN' },
  knowsAbout: ['LLM evaluation', 'Benchmarks', 'Static analysis', 'Verification of AI-generated code'],
  sameAs: [site.github, site.linkedin],
};
---
<Base jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1>{site.headline}</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a final-year computer science student at {site.school} in {site.city}, graduating in {site.graduation}.
        Most of my work is about one kind of bug: output that passes its checks and is still wrong.
        A coding agent says it finished and left a function out. A safety gate is written but never called.
        A model loads without an error and predicts the same class for every image.
        I build the benchmarks and static checks that find these, and I report what they miss.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm looking for AI/ML engineering internships and entry-level roles, in India, remote, Japan, Europe, the US, or Canada.
      </p>
      <ContactLinks />
    </div>
    <Image
      class="portrait"
      src={photo}
      alt="Portrait of Avnish Singh"
      widths={[176, 352, 528]}
      sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 112px, 176px"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </section>

  <p class="evidence">
    Every highlighted number on this site is a link to the file, test run, or commit it came from.
    For example, OmitBench passes <Claim id="ob.tests" /> tests. Follow the link to check.
  </p>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="now">
    <h2 id="now">Now</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="muted">{site.now.date}.</span> I'm building AgentGrade, deterministic guardrails and a Python evaluation harness for a Salesforce Agentforce agent.
      Its most useful result so far is a silent failure of its own: gate logic in Agent Script that validates cleanly and then never runs.
      The integrity analyzer preprint is written, and arXiv submission is pending.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="section" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <h2 id="work-heading">Selected work</h2>

    <article class="work">
      <header>
        <h3><a href="/work/omitbench/">OmitBench</a></h3>
        <span class="muted">2026</span>
      </header>
      <p class="lede">A benchmark for silent omissions in coding-agent patches.</p>
      <p>
        On <Claim id="ob.instances" /> instances built by mutating real merged commits, my deterministic detector beat a grep baseline
        and a reasoning LLM judge, then lost to a mid-tier LLM judge by an MCC difference of <Claim id="ob.delta.b5" />,
        with a 95% interval that excludes zero. I kept that as the headline, and shipped my detector anyway as a CI gate,
        because a gate that cries wolf gets switched off.
      </p>
      <MccChart />
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="/work/omitbench/">Case study</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Avnish1505/Omitbench">Code</a></li>
        <li><a href={posts[0].href}>Write-up</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="work">
      <header>
        <h3><a href="/work/integrity-analyzer/">Implementation Integrity Analyzer</a></h3>
        <span class="muted">2026</span>
      </header>
      <p class="lede">Static analysis for safety checks that AI-generated code defines but never calls.</p>
      <p>
        While building AegisOps AI with a coding assistant, I caught it scaffolding the safety gate twice without wiring it in.
        This analyzer looks for that failure. On a benchmark of <Claim id="iia.scenarios" /> scenarios it reaches MCC <Claim id="iia.mcc" />,
        with precision <Claim id="iia.precision" /> and recall <Claim id="iia.recall" />.
        A name search catches nothing, because a function's name always appears in its own definition.
      </p>
      <ConfusionGrid />
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="/work/integrity-analyzer/">Case study</a></li>
        <li><a href={papers.iia.pdf}>Preprint</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Avnish1505/aegisops-ai">Code</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="work">
      <header>
        <h3><a href="/work/cancer-fusion/">Cancer Fusion AI</a></h3>
        <span class="muted">2026</span>
      </header>
      <p class="lede">A skin lesion classifier that combines dermoscopy images with patient metadata.</p>
      <p>
        Macro-F1 <Claim id="cf.test.macroF1" /> on <Claim id="cf.test.n" /> held-out test images, and <Claim id="cf.valMacroF1" /> on the
        validation set used to pick the checkpoint. Melanoma recall is <Claim id="cf.test.melRecall" /> at precision <Claim id="cf.test.melPrecision" />, so I treat it as a triage filter, not a diagnosis.
        The bug I learned the most from was silent: a stale checkpoint loaded without an error, and the model predicted one class for every image.
      </p>
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="/work/cancer-fusion/">Case study</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Avnish1505/cancer-fusion-ai">Code</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
    <h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>
    <ul class="entries">
      <li>
        <a class="entry-title" href={papers.iia.pdf}>{papers.iia.title}</a>
        <span class="muted">{papers.iia.authors}. {papers.iia.venue}</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="entry-title" href={papers.law.pdf}>{papers.law.title}</a>
        <span class="muted">{papers.law.authors}. {papers.law.venue}</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
    <h2 id="writing-heading">Writing</h2>
    <ul class="entries">
      {posts.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <a class="entry-title" href={post.href}>{post.title}</a>
          <span class="muted">{post.date}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 2rem 2.75rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.05rem, 1.35rem + 3.3vw, 3.35rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.026em;
    font-weight: 660;
    max-width: 20ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro p {
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .intro :global(.links) {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .portrait {
    width: 176px;
    height: 176px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    filter: saturate(0.9);
  }
  .evidence {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .evidence :global(.claim) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .work {
    margin-top: 2.6rem;
  }
  .work:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .work header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .work h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
  .work h3 a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .work h3 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .work header .muted {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .entries {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }
  .entries li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .entry-title {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 560;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .entry-title:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .entries .muted {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .portrait {
      grid-row: 1;
      width: 112px;
      height: 112px;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
